        summary: "Mandiant (Google Cloud) brings frontline incident-response data to the AI-threat picture, and its central finding maps directly onto this playbook: the most pressing AI risks aren't exotic model-theft attacks but foundational gaps, Shadow AI, missing AIBOMs, weak IT hygiene, and excessive agency (agents with overly broad permissions). Its conclusion that root causes are 'rarely novel AI-specific attacks, but rather basic implementation flaws and missing IT hygiene' is the assume-breach / agents-as-insiders / containment thesis, validated by real engagements. Pairs with GTIG's tracking of adversaries operationalizing AI (e.g., the TeamPCP supply-chain compromises).",
