        summary: "The foundational US framework for trustworthy AI (NIST AI 100-1, Jan 2023), voluntary and widely adopted across the federal public sector and beyond. It organizes AI risk management into four functions: GOVERN, MAP, MEASURE, MANAGE, and defines the characteristics of trustworthy AI. The GenAI Profile (600-1) extends it and the Cybersecurity Framework (CSF 2.0) runs alongside it; together they form the NIST backbone a federal-facing program is expected to align to.",
