        summary: "RAITE (Robust Artificial Intelligence Test Event) is a U.S. Navy AI test-and-evaluation exercise run by Naval Surface Warfare Center Crane. It brings government and industry together for time-boxed, hackathon-style exercises where teams alternate Red (attacker) and Blue (defender) roles against live AI/ML systems to find and expose vulnerabilities before fielding; the 2026 event was held at Playas, New Mexico. An industry red team fielded a cross-functional 'Fusion Cell' built on a deliberate people-over-products philosophy (their framing: 'Crew Over COTS'), building custom attacks on-site with AI-assisted coding rather than relying on a pre-packaged toolkit. Across three red-team scenarios: a computer-vision person-detector, a GenAI/LLM application, and a full-spectrum critical-infrastructure target, the team's self-reported results make this the playbook's most direct account of human-led adversarial AI testing in a federal setting. (Source: John Herren, \"What RAITE 2026 Taught Us About Mission-Ready AI\"; specifics as reported by the author.)",
